{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.mkInstanceNameOfType\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Command</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkInstanceNameOfType</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">type</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">avoid</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Environment.html#Lean.Environment\">Environment</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></span> := <span class=\"fn\">fun (<span class=\"fn\">env</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Environment.html#Lean.Environment\">Environment</a>) (<span class=\"fn\">name</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>) =&gt; <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">env</span>.<a href=\"./Lean/Environment.html#Lean.Environment.contains\">contains</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">name</span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Term/TermElabM.html#Lean.Elab.Term.TermElabM\">TermElabM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Convenience function for determining the fully qualified name of an instance using its type as an\nexpression, returning a private name if the type refers to private constants.\n\n`avoid` can be used to specify precisely which names to avoid; by default this includes just the\nones present in the ambient environment but in some cases, you may need to avoid more; for example\nwhen computing names of many instances at once without already knowing the values of them.\n\nThis function is meant to be used for computing the instance name for generated instances in meta\ncode.","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.mkInstanceNameOfType","kind":"def","line":282,"name":"Lean.Elab.Command.mkInstanceNameOfType","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.lean#L282-L302"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.mkInstanceName\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Command</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkInstanceName</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">binders</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Syntax\">Syntax</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">type</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Syntax\">Syntax</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Command.html#Lean.Elab.Command.CommandElabM\">CommandElabM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Generates an instance name for a declaration that has the given binders and type.\nIt tries to make these names relatively unique ecosystem-wide.\n\nThe result is just a single component name (potentially with macro scopes). To get the actual\ndeclaration name, the current namespace has to be prepended.\n\nNote that this elaborates the binders and the type.\nThis means that when elaborating an instance declaration, we elaborate these twice.\n\nThis function is used during elaboration of `instance` declarations to bring it into the same shape\nas other usual `def`s. For instances that are instead generated from meta code, use\n`mkInstanceNameOfType` instead.","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.mkInstanceName","kind":"def","line":258,"name":"Lean.Elab.Command.mkInstanceName","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.lean#L258-L280"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.NameGen.mkBaseNameWithSuffix'\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Command</span>.<span class=\"name\">NameGen</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkBaseNameWithSuffix'</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">pre</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">binders</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Syntax\">Syntax</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">type</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Syntax\">Syntax</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Term/TermElabM.html#Lean.Elab.Term.TermElabM\">TermElabM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Elaborates the binders and type and then uses `mkBaseNameWithSuffix` to generate a name.\nFurthermore, uses `mkUnusedBaseName` on the result.\n\nThe result is just a single component name (potentially with macro scopes). To get the actual\ndeclaration name, the current namespace has to be prepended.","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.NameGen.mkBaseNameWithSuffix'","kind":"def","line":239,"name":"Lean.Elab.Command.NameGen.mkBaseNameWithSuffix'","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.lean#L239-L254"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.NameGen.mkBaseNameWithSuffix\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Command</span>.<span class=\"name\">NameGen</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkBaseNameWithSuffix</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">pre</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">type</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Uses heuristics to generate an informative but terse base name for a term of the given type, using `mkBaseName`.\nMakes use of the current namespace but does not prepend it to the output.\nIt tries to make these names relatively unique ecosystem-wide,\nand it adds suffixes using the current module if the resulting name doesn't refer to anything defined in this module.\n\nIf any constant in `type` has a name with macro scopes, then the result will be a name with fresh macro scopes.\nWhile in this case we could skip the naming heuristics, we still want informative names for debugging purposes.","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.html#Lean.Elab.Command.NameGen.mkBaseNameWithSuffix","kind":"def","line":210,"name":"Lean.Elab.Command.NameGen.mkBaseNameWithSuffix","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Elab/DeclNameGen.lean#L210-L237"}}],"imports":["Init.Data.String.Modify","Init.Omega","Lean.Elab.Command"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Elab.DeclNameGen"}